      en: "Rockley is a coastal resort in Christ Church, Barbados, featuring a 1 km sandy beach known as Rockley Beach or Accra Beach. The beach is composed of fine white sand and slopes gently into the sea. The coast is protected by a fringing reef. The area has a tropical climate with average highs of 30°C. Rockley was developed on former agricultural land. The beachfront is lined with hotels and condominiums. The Rockley Golf Club has an 18-hole course. The area experiences a high water table, and drainage systems manage stormwater. Coral reefs support diverse marine life.",
